source: lib/kunit/test.c prints suite attributes (incl. module) before the plan line
   166		 */
   167		pr_info(KUNIT_SUBTEST_INDENT "KTAP version 1\n");
   168		pr_info(KUNIT_SUBTEST_INDENT "# Subtest: %s\n",
   169			  suite->name);
   170		kunit_print_attr((void *)suite, false, KUNIT_LEVEL_CASE);
   171		pr_info(KUNIT_SUBTEST_INDENT "1..%zd\n",
   172			  kunit_suite_num_test_cases(suite));
   173	}
conclusion: the composite object proxy-consumer-kunit-test.o gives KBUILD_MODNAME=proxy_consumer_kunit_test,
            so the KTAP label appears even for a built-in (obj-y) build; MODULE_OBJECT_COUNT and
            CONFIGURED_AS_M decide modularity, and both say built-in.

